# Line endings are LF everywhere, checked out and stored. Without this a Windows checkout converts
# text to CRLF, and oxfmt is LF-only, so `pnpm fmt --check` fails on every file, on a Windows
# contributor's machine and on the Windows CI leg alike. The macOS release and the Linux runner were
# never exposed to it, which is why this was missing while the app was macOS only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. The icons, the fonts and the rendered docs carry bytes that a line
# ending rewrite would corrupt.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
